  "notes": "Powers high-end consumer routers like ASUS GT-AX11000 and Netgear RAX80. While the Linux CPU and DSA Ethernet switch work under OpenWrt bcm4908, the wireless transceivers require closed-source proprietary Broadcom binary blobs ('wl.ko') not redistributable in mainline OpenWrt, leaving wireless non-functional or severely degraded on pure open-source builds.",
